  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ is the anhydride of $\\mathrm{HClO}_{4}$. It reacts with water slowly to give perchloric acid.\r\n$\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\longrightarrow \\underset{\\text { Perchloric acid }}{2 \\mathrm{HClO}_{4}}$\r\nIts structure is as follows:\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_che_a41.png\">\r\n\r\nIt is less reactive than other oxides of chlorine and does not react with $P, S,$ coal or paper at room temperature.",
